   "source": [
    "# 5.2. Formatting Meteorological Datasets for UMEP Processing\n",
    "\n",
    "The meteorological file for UMEP should have the default UMEP format. In the UMEP website, it describes “The output format is space-separated and includes time-related variables of year, day of year, hour and minute.” Note that you have to be aware of UTC time. In the parameter of SOLWEIG in section 9, you need to put “UTC offset”. If you are using UTC, then the UTC offset should be 0. If not, you should change this parameter input accordingly. "
   ]
  },
